    "objective": "herdr-gateway's terminal-detail screen reads every coding-agent TUI through one universal visual-shape heuristic (/home/vantt/projects/herdr-gateway/web/src/block-classify.ts) rather than per-agent knowledge. Two independent symptoms point at the same open architecture question: block-classify.ts keeps needing a new narrow signal for each newly-observed UI shape (three signals added across two recent releases, 0.1.18/0.1.19), and the terminal-detail spec's own Open Gaps section says the display-scroll fallback has only ever been verified live against one coding agent, with no fallback designed if a future agent reacts differently. A separate real project (upstreams/collie, vendored under herdr-gateway at /home/vantt/projects/herdr-gateway/upstreams/collie) already built a per-agent semantic grammar for Claude Code specifically instead of a universal heuristic. Should herdr-gateway continue with, and keep extending, the universal heuristic approach, or move toward a per-agent grammar system -- and if the latter, when and how, given the terminal surface must also work for agents herdr-gateway has not yet encountered?",
